  "scope": "The 240 DB-free queue-component trials reproduce the reported race. The separate application extension adds two cancelling actors and a post-checkout observation gate. The 48 historical attributions include 32 affected-version and 16 fixed-version targets; they do not represent 48 separate issues or full database reproductions.",
  "diagnostic_contribution": "Native cancellation counters already expose lost cancellation. Recorded C Task.cancel receiver identities connect each later target to its collected cancelling actor; CoroPerf joins that actor sample to the same actor lifetime creation. This recovers historical issuer identity, not the CPython root cause.",
  "relationship_semantics": "task_cancellation_requested_at is a causal edge between different Task lifetimes. Only the historical cancelling actor sample is joined to its own creation; the actor is not claimed to create the target.",
